<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan to sell sugar cane seeds to Iran.</title>
<headline>Taiwan to sell sugar cane seeds to Iran.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Taiwan Sugar Company has agreed to sell an unspecified amount of sugar cane seeds to Iran in mid-February, the economics ministry said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>The seeds were ordered by Iran's Karun Argo company, the statement said. It did not give further details.</p>
<p>Taiwan Sugar has exported sugar cane seeds to the Philippines, Japan and Vietnam.</p>
<p>Taiwan and Iran do not have diplomatic ties.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
